1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,913
What if objects remembered everyone who touched them?

2
00:00:03,953 --> 00:00:05,590
In a dusty antique shop,

3
00:00:05,630 --> 00:00:07,546
you pick up an old blue mug,

4
00:00:07,586 --> 00:00:10,760
and a crowd of glowing ghostly figures appears

5
00:00:10,800 --> 00:00:13,415
behind you, each holding the same mug.

6
00:00:14,050 --> 00:00:15,348
Doorknobs are worse.

7
00:00:15,388 --> 00:00:18,090
A thousand hands squeeze the same knob in

8
00:00:18,130 --> 00:00:21,368
a glowing queue that stretches around the corner.

9
00:00:21,408 --> 00:00:23,174
You only want to go inside,

10
00:00:23,214 --> 00:00:25,850
and the ghosts politely wait their turn.

11
00:00:26,750 --> 00:00:28,797
A coin flashes through town.

12
00:00:28,837 --> 00:00:31,779
You can see its whole journey in glowing

13
00:00:31,819 --> 00:00:33,941
footsteps: a busker, a baker,

14
00:00:33,981 --> 00:00:35,432
a child, a magician,

15
00:00:35,472 --> 00:00:36,401
and now, you.

16
00:00:36,441 --> 00:00:38,563
Nobody ever kept it for long.

17
00:00:39,050 --> 00:00:42,160
In the elevator, the button glows with everyone

18
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:43,433
who ever pushed it.

19
00:00:43,473 --> 00:00:45,712
Impatient ghosts jab it ten times.

20
00:00:45,752 --> 00:00:47,588
Polite ghosts tap it gently.

21
00:00:47,628 --> 00:00:51,274
One suspicious ghost just keeps staring at the ceiling.

22
00:00:51,750 --> 00:00:55,268
Back home, your old teddy bear remembers everything.

23
00:00:55,308 --> 00:00:57,526
A tiny glowing you hugs it on the

24
00:00:57,566 --> 00:00:58,894
first day of school.

25
00:00:58,934 --> 00:01:01,562
Another glowing you hugs it after a bad

26
00:01:01,602 --> 00:01:04,915
dream, and another after your very first goodbye.

27
00:01:05,850 --> 00:01:08,634
Scientists say atoms can't remember anything,

28
00:01:08,674 --> 00:01:10,955
so this is just a thought experiment.

29
00:01:10,995 --> 00:01:14,343
Still, imagine every object quietly holding the warmth

30
00:01:14,383 --> 00:01:16,163
of the hands that touched it.

31
00:01:16,650 --> 00:01:17,743
Here's the twist.

32
00:01:17,783 --> 00:01:20,477
In Grandma's sewing box you find a silver

33
00:01:20,517 --> 00:01:22,811
thimble, and it remembers her best.

34
00:01:22,851 --> 00:01:24,878
A soft glowing Grandma appears,

35
00:01:24,918 --> 00:01:28,478
stitching a scarf, humming the song she always hummed.

36
00:01:28,950 --> 00:01:31,376
She puts her glowing hand over yours,

37
00:01:31,416 --> 00:01:33,109
and for one gentle moment,

38
00:01:33,149 --> 00:01:34,642
you can almost feel it.

39
00:01:34,682 --> 00:01:36,642
Maybe nothing truly leaves us.

40
00:01:36,682 --> 00:01:39,241
Maybe the world just keeps every touch,

41
00:01:39,281 --> 00:01:41,241
softly, in the things we love.
